ed_at":"2026-09-27T21:04:50Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArduPilot/APReview","visibility":"public","watchers":0,"watchers_count":0,"web_commit_signoff_required":false},"sha":"7b2ce6dc676a26147e1a5da0232c89b36e5c12a2","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17919847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ArduPilot","id":17919847,"login":"ArduPilot","node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE3OTE5ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot/subscriptions","type":"Organization","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArduPilot","user_view_type":"public"}},"body":"The ArduPilot subscription pays for ArduPilot reviews and a personal one pays for the rest, so an account is a property of the task, not of the box. It was previously one hardcoded variable for one mode, which does not survive either running out of weekly quota or a second Codex account.\r\n\r\nEach account is now a directory under $REVIEW_ROOT/auth - a CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or a CODEX_HOME - and a symlink per role says which account that role uses:\r\n\r\n  auth/claude-default -> claude-ardupilot     every ArduPilot task\r\n  auth/claude-rsync   -> claude-personal      the non-ArduPilot target\r\n  auth/codex-default  -> codex-personal\r\n  auth/codex-rsync    -> codex-personal\r\n\r\nSwitching is repointing a symlink: `review-auth.sh use claude default personal` moves the whole workload to the other subscription and the next run picks it up. review-auth.sh also reports what every role resolves to and what each directory is signed in as, and prints the login command for a new one. A role with no symlink falls back to default, so a new role costs nothing until it needs its own account. Nothing under auth/ is in git.\r\n\r\nThe guard changes meaning with it. It no longer enforces one address per mode, because which account a role uses is now the operator's choice; it enforces that the directory is signed in, and matches the address recorded in its ACCOUNT file if it has one - the case that otherwise looks exactly like success.\r\n\r\nTwo things found while building it, both by running it rather than reading it. Setting CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR to the tool's own default directory is not a no-op: `claude auth status` then reports loggedIn with no address, because the address lives in <dir>/.claude.json and only a directory created by `claude auth login` under that variable has one. A first draft would have refused every ArduPilot run as \"not signed in\". So a role resolving to ~/.claude leaves the variable unset, identity is read from the directory's own record first, and \"signed in, address unknown\" is accepted rather than treated as a failure.\r\n\r\nrunner/tests/test_auth_roles.py covers the resolution through bash: a role resolves to its own symlink, an unset role falls back to default, no default means no answer rather than a wrong one, the two tools do not share a role, and the resolved path is the real one - which run-reviewprs.sh depends on to decide whether to set the variable at all.","changed_files":14,"closed_at":"2026-09-19T07:10:43Z","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArduPilot/APReview/issues/2/comments","commits":16,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArduPilot/APReview/pulls/2/commits","created_at":"2026-09-17T05:46:08Z","deletions":146,"diff_url":"https://github.com/ArduPilot/APReview/pull/2.diff","draft"